d2 (0.9.0-2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Rebuild against action-debian-build v1.10.0, which restores
    reproducibility. Upstream ships the man page, so debian/d2.manpages
    names a path in upstream's tree; dh_installman copies it through
    debhelper's install_file, which restores the source's timestamps, and
    gzip carries that onto d2.1.gz. It kept the checkout's mtime here while
    a rebuild from the .dsc took upstream's commit date from the orig
    tarball. dpkg-deb clamps only the newer of the two, so the two builds
    disagreed by one tar header.

 -- pkg.haus archive <archive@pkg.haus>  Wed, 16 Sep 2026 14:30:46 +0200

